# `npm test` compares every committed .js against a fresh Babel build of its
# .jsx, and Babel always writes LF. A Windows checkout with Git's default
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF, which fails that check on every
# file it has rewritten — and because Git only rewrites files a pull actually
# touches, the failure shows up as a puzzling subset rather than all of them.
# Pin the line endings here instead of depending on each machine's Git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.ico     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks     binary
*.aab     binary
*.apk     binary
